{"page":"CSRP3","gene":"CSRP3","accession":"P50461","protein":"Cysteine and glycine-rich protein 3","length":194,"events":["Alternative splicing"],"canonical":{"accession":"P50461-1","name":"1","synonyms":["MLP-a"],"notes":[],"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000265968.9","ENST00000533783.2","ENST00000649235.1","ENST00000862857.1","ENST00000862858.1","ENST00000862859.1","ENST00000862860.1","ENST00000951069.1","ENST00000951071.1","ENST00000951072.1","ENST00000951073.1","ENST00000951075.1"],"refseq":["NM_003476.5"],"refseqProteins":["NP_003467.1"],"maneSelect":true,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"model":{"entry":"AF-P50461-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P50461-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":73.4,"plddt":[[0,1],[50,5],[70,3],[90,1],[70,19],[90,2],[70,1],[90,5],[70,2],[90,1],[70,1],[90,3],[70,5],[90,1],[70,5],[90,4],[70,9],[50,20],[0,3],[50,1],[0,7],[50,1],[0,3],[50,1],[0,2],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1],[0,3],[50,1],[0,1],[50,3],[70,22],[90,2],[70,3],[90,3],[70,2],[90,1],[70,15],[90,3],[70,10],[50,1],[0,1],[50,2],[0,7],[50,1],[0,2],[50,1],[0,1]]}},"features":[{"type":"Region","start":1,"end":5,"description":"Interaction with TCAP"},{"type":"Domain","start":10,"end":61,"description":"LIM zinc-binding 1"},{"type":"Motif","start":64,"end":69,"description":"Nuclear localization signal"},{"type":"Region","start":94,"end":105,"description":"Interaction with CLF2 and isoform 2"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":95,"end":95,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Domain","start":120,"end":171,"description":"LIM zinc-binding 2"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":153,"end":153,"description":"Phosphoserine"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Self-associates. Oligomeric in the cytoplasm and monomeric in the nucleus (By similarity). Homooligomers preferentially form along the actin cytoskeleton. Isoform 2 interacts with isoform 1 (PubMed:24860983, PubMed:24934443). Isoform 1 but not isoform 2 interacts with MYOD1 and MYOG. Isoform 1 interacts with TCAP, ACTN2 and NRAP. Isoform 2 interacts with TCAP and alpha-actinin (PubMed:12507422, PubMed:15205937, PubMed:15582318, PubMed:24860983). Interacts with LDHD. Interacts (via N-terminus)with GLRX3 (via C-terminus) and PPP3CA; GLRX3 and calcineurin compete for interaction with CSRP3. Interacts with MYF6 (By similarity). Interacts with CFL2; the stoichiometry influences F-actin depolymerization and possibly two molecules of CFL2 can interact with one molecule of CSRP3 resulting in the highest functional impact; the interaction is stronger with phosphorylated CFL2 (PubMed:19752190)"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"P50461-2","name":"2","synonyms":["MLP-b"],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"May play a role in early sarcomere organization. Overexpression in myotubes negatively regulates myotube differentiation. By association with isoform 1 and thus changing the CSRP3 isoform 1:CFL2 stoichiometry is proposed to down-regulate CFL2-mediated F-actin depolymerization"}],"length":58,"transcripts":{"ensembl":[],"refseq":[],"refseqProteins":[],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,37]],"edits":[{"start":38,"end":194,"original":"MACRKALDSTTVAAHESEIYCKVCYGRRYGPKGIGYGQGA","replacement":"TLAQDLFPLCHLWEESGVHKC","added":21}],"missing":157,"replaced":0,"novel":21,"foldedAbsent":92,"foldedMissing":92,"features":[[1,24,0],[2,6,0],[3,12,0],[4,1,0],[5,52,0],[6,1,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-P50461-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P50461-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":69.3,"plddt":[[0,2],[50,3],[70,4],[90,1],[70,2],[90,1],[70,1],[90,2],[70,14],[90,1],[70,5],[50,18],[0,1],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1]],"losingConfidence":0}}],"ensemblGenes":["ENSG00000129170.11"],"unmapped":{"ensembl":[],"refseq":[],"refseqProteins":[]},"coding":{"genes":[{"id":"ENSG00000129170","name":"CSRP3","chromosome":"chr11","readthrough":false}],"gencode":18,"mapped":12},"explorer":{"gene":null,"isoforms":"CSRP3"},"locus":"chr11:19176519-19210571","exons":{"transcript":"ENST0000